@startuml
title Domain Model Excerpt — US031 (BackOffice Operator Registration)

skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor<<AggregateRoot>> #D0C8F8
    BorderColor<<AggregateRoot>> #534AB7
    BackgroundColor<<ValueObject>> #FAE8C0
    BorderColor<<ValueObject>> #854F0B
    BackgroundColor<<FrameworkEntity>> #C8F0D0
    BorderColor<<FrameworkEntity>> #1A7A34
    BackgroundColor<<Builder>> #F0F4C3
    BorderColor<<Builder>> #827717
}

package "EAPLI Framework (Authentication Layer)" {
    class SystemUser <<FrameworkEntity>> {
        + username : Username
        + password : Password
        + roles : RoleSet
        + active : boolean
        + isActive(): boolean
    }
}

package "AlSafe Domain (User Management Aggregate)" {
    class User <<AggregateRoot>> {
        + email : EmailAddress
        + name : String
        + phoneNumber : String
        + staffNumber : String
        + active : boolean
        + role : String
        + securityClearanceExpiry : LocalDate
        + nextSkillsAssessmentDate : LocalDate
    }

    class UserExceptionBuilder <<Builder>> {
        + {static} of(...): UserExceptionBuilder
        + validate(): void
    }

    class EmailAddress <<ValueObject>> {
        + address : String
    }

    User "1" *-- "1" EmailAddress
    User ..> UserExceptionBuilder : delegates validation
}

SystemUser .. User : linked by email\n(username = email)

note right of User
  Domain invariants (enforced by UserExceptionBuilder):
  - email unique, valid format, valid AlSafe domain
  - name not blank
  - phoneNumber exactly 9 digits, unique
  - staffNumber not blank, unique
  - securityClearanceExpiry must be future
  - nextSkillsAssessmentDate = today + 5yr (auto)
  - active = true on creation
  - role = "BACKOFFICE_OPERATOR" on creation
    (Admin can only create BackOffice Operators)
  Note: password and authentication
  managed by SystemUser (framework)
end note

note right of UserExceptionBuilder
  Accumulates all validation violations.
  Throws IllegalArgumentException only at
  validate() — after all checks run.
  Keeps User constructor free of guard clauses.
  User is always validated BEFORE SystemUser
  is created, preventing orphan records.
end note

note left of SystemUser
  Managed by EAPLI Framework.
  Stores credentials and roles.
  Created via UserManagementService,
  but ONLY after domain User is validated.
end note
@enduml
